a8b9e413863c0", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01UkuvuoYuLracWPzMdjuxF3", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/deliver; git pull -q --ff-only 2>&1|tail -1; git log --oneline | head -2; git diff 2a7f2fc HEAD --stat | tail -5; git diff 2a7f2fc HEAD -- paper | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-700", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/deliver; git pull -q --ff-only 2>&1|tail -1; git log --oneline | head -2; git diff 2a7f2fc HEAD --stat | tail -5; git diff 2a7f2fc HEAD -- paper | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-700"]], "output": "```console\nb94fa37 Coverage by family on all 1800 cells; median gap 0.40-0.53 (analysis' review of candidate 2)\n2a7f2fc Coverage by family: say on which cells\n paper/sections/results.tex | 4 ++--\n 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n--- a/paper/sections/results.tex\n+++ b/paper/sections/results.tex\n-The population-OLS prediction of the bias (Eq.~\\ref{eq:bias}; exact in form, it uses the true response and the realised graph) lies inside the Monte Carlo interval of the measured bias in 85.1\\% of 1224 cells, and in 86.7\\% with the finite-$n$ centring of the fit, which we added after only 81\\% of the cells of the diffusion mechanism (e) were inside (90\\% with it). The median absolute gap is 0.39--0.53 of the Monte Carlo half-width by mechanism, the largest gap 0.016--0.052 in bias units, the mean about zero; the data do not separate predictor error from interval error as the reason for the shortfall from 95\\%. The median absolute bias over $p$ and $s$ varies by under 15\\% across $d=5,20,80\n+The population-OLS prediction of the bias (Eq.~\\ref{eq:bias}; exact in form, it uses the true response and the realised graph) lies inside the Monte Carlo interval of the measured bias in 85.1\\% of 1224 cells, and in 86.7\\% with the finite-$n$ centring of the fit, which we added after only 81\\% of the cells of the diffusion mechanism (e) were inside (90\\% with it). The median absolute gap is 0.40--0.53 of the Monte Carlo half-width by mechanism, the largest gap 0.016--0.052 in bias units, the mean about zero; the data do not separate predictor error from interval error as the reason for the shortfall from 95\\%. The median absolute bias over $p$ and $s$ varies by under 15\\% across $d=5,20,80\n-The 95\\% HC0 interval of the regression covers the true GATE in 73.6\\% of the 1800 Bernoulli cells of Figure~\\ref{fig:cov}. Coverage is set by the size of the bias relative to the SD and not by leverage: the mean is 93\\%, 92\\%, 87\\%, 67\\% and 16\\% for $|{\\rm bias}|/{\\rm SD}$ in $\\le0.25$, 0.25--0.5, 0.5--1, 1--2 and $>2$. Among cells with $|{\\rm bias}|/{\\rm SD}<0.25$ coverage is 94\\%, 93\\%, 90\\% and 95\\% by quartile of $L$: leverage costs a few points at most. On these cells, by graph family, coverage is lowest on Stanford3 (0.52) and ego-Facebook (0.66) and highest on Watts--Strogatz (0.82). The bootstrap interval for DM, centred on an estimate biased by $-s\\gate$, covers in fewer than 0.1\n+The 95\\% HC0 interval of the regression covers the true GATE in 73.6\\% of the 1800 Bernoulli cells of Figure~\\ref{fig:cov}. Coverage is set by the size of the bias relative to the SD and not by leverage: the mean is 93\\%, 92\\%, 87\\%, 67\\% and 16\\% for $|{\\rm bias}|/{\\rm SD}$ in $\\le0.25$, 0.25--0.5, 0.5--1, 1--2 and $>2$. Among cells with $|{\\rm bias}|/{\\rm SD}<0.25$ coverage is 94\\%, 93\\%, 90\\% and 95\\% by quartile of $L$: leverage costs a few points at most. On all 1800 cells, by graph family, coverage is lowest on Stanford3 (0.52) and ego-Facebook (0.66) and highest on Watts--Strogatz (0.82). The bootstrap interval for DM, centred on an estimate biased by $-s\\gate$, covers in fewer than\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "bf6162b0-2fda-53cb-95a8-7d4e5cfc10e2", "at": 1795654523.943175, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 1143